en-names></name><name><surname>Courtneidge</surname><given-names>S.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>van Obberghen-Schilling</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name></person-group><source>J. Biol. Chem</source><volume>269</volume><year>1994</year><fpage>27372</fpage><lpage>27377</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7525555</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Chereshetal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cheresh</surname><given-names>D.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Leng</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Klemke</surname><given-names>R.L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulation of cell contraction and membrane ruffling by distinct signals in migratory cells</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol</source><volume>146</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>1107</fpage><lpage>1116</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10477763</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Chewetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chew</surname><given-names>T.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Masaracchia</surname><given-names>R.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Goeckeler</surname><given-names>Z.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wysolmerski</surname><given-names>R.B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phosphorylation of non-muscle myosin II regulatory light chain by p21-activated kinase (&#x003b3;-PAK)</article-title><source>J. Muscle Res. Cell Motil.</source><volume>19</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>839</fpage><lpage>854</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10047984</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ChungandFirtel1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chung</surname><given-names>C.Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Firtel</surname><given-names>R.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>PAKa, a putative PAK family member, is required for cytokinesis and the regulation of the cytoskeleton in <italic>Dictyostelium discoideum</italic> cells during chemotaxis</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol</source><volume>147</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>559</fpage><lpage>576</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10545500</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CreasyandChernoff1995"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Creasy</surname><given-names>C.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Chernoff</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cloning and characterization of a member of the MST subfamily of Ste20-like protein kinases</article-title><source>Gene</source><volume>167</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>306</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8566796</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="DanielsandBokoch1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Daniels</surname><given-names>R.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bokoch</surname><given-names>G.M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>p21-activated protein kinasea crucial component of morphological signaling?</article-title><source>Trends Biochem.</source><volume>24</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>350</fpage><lpage>355</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Dharmawardhaneetal1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dharmawardhane</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanders</surname><given-names>L.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>S.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Daniels</surname><given-names>R.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bokoch</surname><given-names>G.M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Localization of p21-activated kinase 1 (Pak1) to pinocytotic vesicles and cortical actin structures in stimulated cells</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol</source><volume>138</volume><year>199